# Fantasy Copilot, Cursor rules

Read AGENTS.md first. It is the full brief: architecture, commands, testing conventions and the
twelve rules this project is built around. CLAUDE.md is a shorter version of the same thing.

This is an existing working repo, nine of the thirteen phases built, 133 tests passing.
Finish it, do not redesign it.

## Commands

- `npm test` runs 133 checks with no database and no network
- `npx tsc --noEmit` typechecks
- `npm run build` builds
- `npm run backtest 2024` measures the projection model against a real season
- All three of test, typecheck and build must pass before anything is called done

## Non-negotiable

- `src/lib/core/` stays pure: no Prisma, no Next, no React, no npm dependencies, and no relative
  imports between core modules. Each file stands alone so it can be unit tested with no build
  step. `npm run test:boundaries` enforces it.
- All decision logic lives in core, with tests. Services load rows and call core. Components
  render.
- Tools are defined once, in `src/lib/tools/registry.ts`. Chat and MCP both read that array.
  Never create a second list.
- The LLM explains, it never computes. No projection, rank or probability comes from a language
  model.
- Never write a raw colour utility. No `bg-white/5`, `text-black`, `bg-emerald-500/15`. Use a
  design token, a `tone` prop, or a `.tint-*` class. See DESIGN.md.
- Nothing about league format is hardcoded. Scoring, roster slots, team count, playoff settings
  and replacement level all derive from the synced league.
- No paid APIs and no required API keys. Free public data only.
- Never claim accuracy you have not backtested.

## Style

Human readable, intern level. Clear names, comments only where the logic is not obvious. No
clever metaprogramming. Do not add dependencies; this runs on Next, Prisma, Tailwind and zod
deliberately.
